INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,status,url_slug,created_at,updated_at) VALUES
('polterghast','Polterghast','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"polterghast","name":"Polterghast","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose a player: they die. Once per game, at night*, you may choose to register as dead & poison 1 Townsfolk neighbour.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Over my dead body'', you say? Well, if you insist.","lede":"The Polterghast plays dead.","howToRun":["Consider running this Demon on scripts where multiple deaths in the night are common. Tinker, Gambler, Gossip, Assassin or Acrobat, for instance, are great roles to pair with a Polterghast and enables them to make the most of their ability without being found out easily."],"tips":["You are a Demon with slices of the reality-bending power of the Zombuul, and the poisoning power of a Vigormortis, but with greater agility and flexibility. Use it to your advantage! Bluffing roles like the Gossip or Gambler enable you to sell a world where you have died to your ability, and push suspicion on to others while also corrupting information around town. Choosing when to activate your unique ability - and how - lets you control the narrative of the game.","You can, for instance, “die” during the night alongside another Townsfolk to sell an otherwise difficult Gambler or Tinker bluff; or you can sink a kill on an already dead player and use your ability to register as the only death during the night. Doing so may steer town away from a world where a Polterghast even exists!","Adapt your playstyle to the situation and know when it’s time to go, and the Polterghast becomes an incredibly strong Demon to pin down."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Polterghasts will frequently bluff roles that may die in the night given certain circumstances, so follow their claims closely. If their gossips or gambles sound implausible, there’s a good chance they’re bluffing about the reasons for their death in the night.","Similarly, as opposed to a Vigormortis where poisoned Townsfolk simply point to killed Minions, poisoned Townsfolk may give you a direct line to the Demon itself!","Also consider that until a Polterghast activates their ability, they are a stationary, “normal” Demon, so you only need to start worrying about whether a Polterghast is pulling tricks until viable candidates have died in the night."],"examples":["Kimberly is the Polterghast claiming to be the Gossip. With seven players remaining, they gossip that the Demon is one specific player. They use their ability at night, poisoning their neighbour, and kill elsewhere.","Bobby is the Fortune Teller with a yes on a claimed Tinker. The Tinker appears to die at night. Bobby nominates the dead Tinker, just to make sure. Bobby was right."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":37,"otherNightReminder":"The Polterghast chooses a player . They may also choose to use their ability to feign death. Give them the ''Play Dead'' token and announce them as dead in the morning.","reminders":["Dead","Play Dead","Poisoned"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Scarlet Woman","align":"good","text":"If the Polterghast dies while registering as dead, the Scarlet Woman becomes the Polterghast whose ability has already been used.","id":"scarletwoman"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/pole.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/polg.png"}','published','the-menagerie/polterghast',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('seiren','Seiren','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"seiren","name":"Seiren","team":"demon","ability":"Each night, choose a player: they become your alignment. The previously changed player dies: they swap back before dawn, even if the Seiren is drunk. Anyone ''mad'' about being evil might be executed. [-1 Minion]","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"It is said their song is honey-sweet, carried on rotten air. Among the salt and carrion, it is a tonic that heals and soothes. Pray you never hear it.","lede":"The Seiren turns players to their team before their final moments.","howToRun":["While the Seiren acts early during the night, the decay of its turning isn’t until dawn for recently dead players. Don’t forget to turn characters back as necessary to ensure that only one remains evil for the next day."],"tips":["The Seiren is an incredibly powerful Demon with the ability to temporarily ‘recruit’ teammates. Early on, this provides you with ample cover from Townsfolk abilities, since a turned player will register as evil to characters such as the Seamstress or Empath. But, later in the game, players turned by the Seiren may have the ability to win the game alongside you and may actively assist you! As you learn more about the game state, consider who you turn and when, as some players may be more inclined to assist than others.","Also remember that because players who are turned register as evil all the way up until dawn, this ensures characters like the Oracle will see them as evil, so don’t be afraid to push on players you turn. But remember that ultimately, those players will be able to confess that they were only temporarily evil, so if you’re too eager, town might figure you out."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["If you suspect a Seiren is in play, be careful about when you use abilities that check alignment, like the Seamstress. You can’t be certain that the information you have is true, even if sober, so try to find other sources of confirmation. Additionally, if you are a character who can get a read on multiple characters at once, you can use the turned player as a starting point, and use it to compare to other players! Did your Seamstress get a ‘yes’ between a turned player and their neighbour? If so, you may reasonably deduce that the neighbour is evil too!"],"examples":["Zoe is the Seiren. They select the Mutant, who neighbours the Recluse. That same night, the Chef receives a 2 instead of a 1.","Teri is the Balloonist who is turned evil on Night 5. On Day 5, just three players remain. Teri realises they must play for evil, so they change their Balloonist pings at the last minute. Sneaky Teri."],"firstNight":41,"firstNightReminder":"The Seiren selects a player: mark them with the ''Turned'' reminder, wake them, and inform them of their new alignment.","otherNight":37,"otherNightReminder":"The Seiren selects a player: mark them with the ''Turned'' reminder, wake them, and inform them of their new alignment. The previously turned character dies; inform them that they are their previous alignment before the next day begins.","reminders":["Turned","Dead"],"setup":true,"jinxes":[{"name":"Evil Twin","align":"good","text":"The Evil Twin''s good player still counts as good for the purposes of the Evil Twin''s ability when turned by the Seiren.","id":"eviltwin"},{"name":"Monk","align":"good","text":"The Monk''s ability fails if they try to protect a player already turned evil by the Seiren. ","id":"monk"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/seie.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/seig.png"}','published','the-menagerie/seiren',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('shogun-the-menagerie','Shogun','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"shogun-the-menagerie","name":"Shogun","team":"demon","ability":"All players know you are the Shogun. Minions & Demons do not know each other. Each day, publicly choose a player: they die. After execution, players may nominate you & if executed while Minions live, your team wins. [+1 Minion, No Outsiders]","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"分をわきまえろ痴者が。","lede":"The Shogun is known to everyone and will take everyone down with him, unless his hidden Minions are killed.","howToRun":["This character uses a lot of jinxes, so be cognisant of them, and remind players about them prior to the game''s commencement.","Consider putting a number of powerful information roles on scripts with the Shogun, as there are far less chances to find and kill evil players."],"tips":["This is the most outed evil a player can be, so enjoy it. Normally being outed as evil is unhelpful, but given that Minions and Demons do not know each other, players will come to you to curry favour and convince you that they are worth keeping around. Use town''s information against them, as their accusations will lead you to your evil team, and see if their stories check out before you brutally kill someone during the day.","Given that you kill during the day, you may opt to forego your ability on Day 1 so that you don''t inadvertently kill a Minion, but perhaps not? The odds of killing a good player are never better, so you may consider going for broke.","Importantly, while Minions are expendable, they are also your only line of defense. Convincing town that your Minions yet live is the only thing keeping them from turning on you, so frame others, be loud, and direct traffic as much as possible."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Remember that roles like the Chef, Town Crier and Empath that locate evil players, or Minions in general, can be harmful to town, as it outs the evil team to the Shogun, or even creates frames the Shogun can lean on to convince town to kill otherwise good players. Keeping information relatively discrete and perhaps even lying about your information might be useful, but finding a balance is essential.","Remember that the Shogun will inevitably kill in final 3, so if you find yourself on the penultimate day, know that you will need to chance it and go for the Shogun!"],"examples":["Alex is the Shogun. He is immediately announced to town, and over the coming days, with 5 players remaining, town is convinced that all Minions are dead. They execute Alex that day, but the Poisoner still lives. Alex''s team wins.","Peter is the General who learns, after several days of evil winning, that the game is now neutral. He chooses to out that evil is still winning to keep a dead Minion hidden. On the day that he learns that good is winning, he correctly discerns that all Minions are dead."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":true,"jinxes":[{"name":"Scarlet Woman","align":"good","text":"The Scarlet Woman cannot become the Demon. Instead, the Scarlet Woman instead gains the ability of the first Minion to die.","id":"scarletwoman"},{"name":"Goblin","align":"good","text":"The Goblin''s ability no longer ends the game. Instead, if the Goblin''s ability would trigger, they may immediately choose a player: they die.","id":"goblin"},{"name":"Mastermind","align":"good","text":"If a Mastermind''s ability would trigger, players must execute a living player that day. If that player is good, evil wins.","id":"mastermind"},{"name":"Spy","align":"good","text":"The Shogun learns who the Spy is. The Spy does not see the Grimoire, but instead learns which Minions are in play.","id":"spy"},{"name":"Widow","align":"good","text":"The Widow learns who the Shogun is. The Widow does not see the Grimoire, but instead learns which Minions are in play.","id":"widow"},{"name":"Boomdandy","align":"good","text":"If the Boomdandy''s ability would trigger, the Shogun must die. Good wins if a Minion is chosen. If the Boomdandy is the only living Minion, the Boomdandy''s ability does not trigger.","id":"boomdandy"},{"name":"Slayer","align":"good","text":"The Slayer can use their ability on Minions.","id":"slayer"},{"name":"Record Keeper","align":"good","text":"If the Record Keeper is executed, the Shogun does not see the Grimoire: they instead learn who their Minions are.","slug":"record-keeper"},{"name":"Poppy Grower","align":"good","text":"The Shogun does not receive bluffs. If the Poppy Grower dies, the Shogun and Minions instead learn players who are dead Minions.","id":"poppygrower"},{"name":"Magician","align":"good","text":"The Magician is also announced as the Shogun. The Shogun must tell the Storyteller who they are killing privately.","id":"magician"},{"name":"Lunatic","align":"good","text":"The Lunatic is also announced as the Shogun. If they target a Minion with their ability, that Minion might die. If they target the Shogun with their ability, their team loses.","id":"lunatic"},{"name":"Mayor","align":"good","text":"If the Mayor is killed by the Demon when 3 players live, the Mayor''s team wins.","id":"mayor"},{"name":"Vizier","align":"good","text":"If the Vizier and Shogun are in play, the Shogun is not announced at the start of the game, but the Vizier is. The Vizier can die during the day.","id":"vizier"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/shoe.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/shog.png"}','published','the-menagerie/shogun',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('umbra','Umbra','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"umbra","name":"Umbra","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose a player: they die. Minions you choose for the first time swap characters with you and poison one Townsfolk neighbour until dusk. [-1 Outsider]","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"People are like shadows. They disappear when it gets dark.","lede":"The Umbra evades execution, moving about the Grimoire, poisoning neighbours in the process.","howToRun":["Balance the game around the Umbra''s poisoning: misinformation in the wrong places can cause the game to become near-unsolvable, so being diligent with where the poisoning lies, and sometimes sending it to dead players, can help temper the Umbra''s power."],"tips":["You are a hyper-mobile Demon who sacrifices deaths at night in order to move about and poison players. Consider utilising Minions that kill like the Muckraker, Assassin or Gerrymanderer to cover your tracks.","Remember that swapping to a Minion does eliminate the \"instance\" of that Minion - so if you''re swapping to your Cerenovus, their madness is removed. But the upside is that swapping to a one-use Minion such as the Necromancer or Assassin renews their ability, meaning they can use it again!","Learning where to swap to in order to guarantee the best poison, and when to swap is essential, so that you are best equipped to win as the Umbra."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Like Demons such as the Vigor Mortis and No Dashii, who poison nearby players, finding sources of poison within a certain proximity is key to defeating the Umbra. If a player wakes to find their information doesn''t quite stack up, there''s a chance they neighbour the new Umbra - so strike while they''re still there. Poisoning in this context is as much a clue as it is a hindrance, but beware other forms of poisoning and drunkenness: it could be an Umbra, but it could also just be a Philosopher who has sadly chosen your ability.","Nights of no deaths are the strongest indicator that an Umbra is about, so use those opportunities to audit your information, and figure out where they could have jumped to."],"examples":["Damien is the Umbra. He selects the Chef on Night 2, who dies. He then selects the Chatterpox on Night 3, poisoning their neighbour, the Seamstress. The Assassin kills that night to cover Damien''s swap.","Nick is the Medicine Man who selects the same two players each night. On Night 3, he learns that one of them has been targeted by poisoning or madness. No deaths occur that night. Nick knows that the Umbra neighbours one of those two players."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":37,"otherNightReminder":"The Umbra selects a player: mark them as dead. - if a Minion is chosen instead and has not been chosen previously, inform the Umbra that they are now that Minion, and wake the Minion to tell them they are now the Umbra. Mark one Townsfolk neighbour as poisoned.","reminders":["Poisoned","Dead"],"setup":true,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/umbe.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/umbg.png"}','published','the-menagerie/umbra',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('yin','Yin','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"yin","name":"Yin","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose a player: they die. If you choose Yang, they become evil, then swap characters with you. If 5 or more players remain and you die, a living Yang becomes an evil Yin-Yang. [-1 Minion, +Yang]","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Water may quell a fire, but in the end, the storm comes, and what is a storm if not water’s surrender to the fire?","lede":"The Yin hunts for its other half, and transforms into something more powerful upon its death.","howToRun":["This is a fairly straightforward Demon, but just remember that if the Yin picks the Yang that you must turn the Yang evil before swapping them with the Yin, to ensure you’ve properly “recruited” the Yang.","The Yang and Yin-Yang must be on the same script as the Yin in order for them to function."],"tips":["Find your other half! With one less Minion to ally yourself with, you are at an immediate disadvantage, however the knowledge that the Yang is out there should give you some reassurance. Finding them allows you to not only recruit them into your ranks, but to be agile, avoiding suspicion through Exorcist abilities, Flowergirl information and the like; and causing confusion as town can’t seem to pin down where demon candidates reside. While finding a Yang does mean that no deaths occur in the night, you can coordinate your actions with a Godfather or Assassin to ensure the extra death at night looks like a normal demon kill, ensuring that town won’t suspect that a Yin/Yang swap has taken place.","Additionally, choosing the Yang at night enables you to swap characters, giving you the versatility of playing as another role, and having control over two aspects of the game.","If there is heavy suspicion on you, feel free to sacrifice yourself to protect your Yang: they will become the Yin-Yang and will carry on the game for you."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Pinning down the Yin’s safety net in the Yang is key to defeating this demon: if you can play patiently and gather information, you can execute the Yang once 4 or fewer players are left alive, ensuring that they cannot jump to the Yang. Look for players who are initially fine to be executed, but become increasingly cautious as time wears on, especially if a Yang is suspected to be found. They may be the recipient of a demon change during the night, and the Yin will not want to let that happen."],"examples":["Eric is the Yin who selects the Politician on Night 2, who dies. He then selects the Yang on Night 3, who becomes the evil Yin; Eric becomes the evil Yang. No-one dies at night.","William is the Seer who received their neighbour, claiming Noble, on Night 1. On Day 4, the Noble is reluctant to die: William discerns they may have been turned evil by the Yin''s ability."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":37,"otherNightReminder":"The Yin chooses a player.","reminders":["Dead","Swap"],"setup":true,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/yine.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/ying.png"}','published','the-menagerie/yin',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('yin-yang','Yin-Yang','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"yin-yang","name":"Yin-Yang","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose two players: at least one, or both, die. Yin learns who you are.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Opposites, when combined, can create something greater than themselves alone.","lede":"The Yin-Yang, as a combined force of its two halves, is more powerful than ever.","howToRun":["Assess the game state before committing to two kills: this will almost certainly out that the Yin-Yang is in play - so if players have heavy suspicion about a particular player, it may be best to stick to single kills until it is most advantageous (ie. if town believes there is a Godfather who may kill after an Outsider death, if town believes there is an unspent Assassin, etc).","Keep in mind that in a Yin/Yang game, the only Demon available at setup is the Yin: the Yin-Yang is a conditional Demon that only appears if the conditions for its creation (outlined in the Yin’s ability) are met."],"tips":["You are a supercharged demon with the ability to kill twice per night with no downsides: use it! Given that the Yin-Yang typically appears later in the game, you have the ability to accelerate the endgame and draw things to a close quickly. As such, lay low, maintain your bluffs, and keep killing at night. If you wish to ensure that town doesn’t know that a Yin-Yang is now in play, you can kill dead players to ensure only one death occurs in the night. Use this false sense of security to turn up the heat later on.","Crucially, the Yin-Yang being in the game means that you definitely know who your other half is: use this to your advantage, support each other (or not, if there is heavy suspicion about!), and coordinate your information to ensure the best possible outcome."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Given the Yin-Yang’s ability to kill twice per night, be prepared for a short endgame. While storytellers will use discretion with regards to who dies at night, you can typically expect multiple kills. Rule out any sources of extra deaths such as the Assassin or Godfather, and re-evaluate your information to figure out who the most suspicious players are. If you’ve confirmed a Yin-Yang is in play, you’ve killed the Yin, and so you know that not only are you close to winning the game, but that there is a guaranteed dead evil player that has less impact on the game moving forward."],"examples":["Gory is the former good Yang, and newly created evil Yin-Yang. Harold, the former Yin, learns who they are. Gory selects two players at night: both die.","Winston is the Undertaker who knows that the Assassin is dead. On Night 4, there are two deaths. They know this can only be the Yin-Yang, and suspect that the player executed on Day 3 may have been the Yin."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":37,"otherNightReminder":"Yin-Yang chooses two players.","reminders":["Dead","Dead"],"setup":false,"special":[{"name":"bag-disabled","type":"selection"}],"jinxes":[{"name":"Hatter","align":"good","text":"The Yin-Yang cannot be swapped to as part of the Hatter''s ability.","id":"hatter"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/yyae.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/yyag.png"}','published','the-menagerie/yin-yang',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('zwei','Zwei','demon','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"zwei","name":"Zwei","team":"demon","ability":"Your good non-Traveler neighbours are poisoned. If the Ein dies, you become the Ein. This can only happen once.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Anderenseites... Das Eichhörnchen ist ein Teufel.","lede":"The Zwei lies in wait, ready to act if the Ein should perish.","howToRun":["The Zwei breaks the usual rule that if more than one Demon lives, kills each night are arbitrary.","Remember the jinx with the Lunatic: if you intend to create a Lunatic Zwei, play with one extra Townsfolk or Outsider token, and claim they have been changed to the Zwei on Night 1.","Keep in mind that in a Ein/Zwei game, the only Demon available at setup is the Ein: the Zwei is selected on the Ein''s first night and cannot be selected on its own."],"tips":["The Ein''s strength is in numbers: while the Zwei doubles the amount of Demons on the Grimoire, making it more susceptible to Demon-finding roles like the Fortune Teller, it also creates an inbuilt Scarlet Woman to pass to should the need arise, and with its own ability to win when 3 players live, as well as the Zwei''s ability to poison its good-aligned neighbours (for better or worse), you have tremendous strength to start, which wanes substantially if it - or you - are killed. While being the Zwei ensures you are at maximum power, remember that you''re the fallback plan, so if you need to push on your Ein to buy credibility down the line, you may need to fall in line with the town''s information.","Your ability to poison good neighbours can set up some interesting interactions, since unlike the No Dashii, you can poison Outsiders, leading to interactions that might have unforseen consequences. Get cosy with your neighbours, learn their roles, and try to use them to your advantage."],"bluffing":[],"fighting":["Two Demons on the board usually spells chaos for the town, but with an Ein in play, it''s business as usual. Double the Demons in play means double the opportunities to find them, so get killing! Executing players who are seen as a viable Demon candidate may weaken the Ein substantially, so don''t bide your time waiting for clarifying information, because you may not have the luxury of a final 3 to decide what is and what isn''t.","You are forced to play offensive to weaken the Ein and ultimately win the game, not just because of its unique win condition, but because your information will be fractured and seemingly unreliable. Once you know it''s in play, don''t delay.","Remember that the Zwei poisons all good players - not just Townsfolk - so while you can build worlds as you would as if a No Dashii is in play, if Outsider abilities like that of the Recluse or Golem don''t seem to work as intended, there''s a good chance a Zwei is nearby."],"examples":["Scott is the Zealot who is chosen by Maurice, the Ein, to be the Zwei. Scott poisons his good neighbours - the Librarian who ultimately confirms him as the Zealot, and the Fortune Teller, who receives correct information, suggesting that Maurice is the Demon, but later receives a no on Scott. Scott rightly pushes on Maurice, who becomes the Ein once Maurice dies, riding his confirmation to a win.","Renee is the Golem. She nominates the claimed Washerwoman, who does not die. The Fisherman, confirmed by the Washerwoman, discerns that they cannot be the Demon given their very first chat together, which confirmed the Washerwoman''s information. Renee correctly determines she is sat next to the Zwei, who forced her power to misfire."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":37.5,"otherNightReminder":"If the Ein died today, wake the Zwei and inform them they are now the Ein.","reminders":["Poisoned","Poisoned"],"setup":false,"special":[{"name":"bag-disabled","type":"selection"}],"jinxes":[{"name":"Lunatic","align":"good","text":"If Lunatic is a Zwei, they start seeing a Townsfolk or Outsider token :reminder:.","id":"lunatic"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/zwee.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/zweg.png"}','published','the-menagerie/zwei',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('mad-scientist','Mad Scientist','traveller','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"mad-scientist","name":"Mad Scientist","team":"traveller","ability":"Each night*, choose a dead player. They are poisoned and alive until dusk.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"It''s alive... it''s alive!","lede":"The Mad Scientist brings the dead back to life... sort of.","howToRun":["If the Mad Scientist chooses a living player, prompt them to choose again."],"tips":["Whether good or evil, the Mad Scientist allows previously dead players to nominate and vote as normal, skewing town''s numbers and keeping the game alive.","In \"end game\" situations where evil wins if a certain number of players live, this can create situations where the Mad Scientist is the last remaining line of defense, giving good one last shot at the Demon, or giving evil a guaranteed win, assuming all evils are left alive.","Bring back players you trust to corroborate (or corrupt!) certain pieces of information in order to maximise their effectiveness.","Also note that if you resurrect a player who was just killed by the Demon, while it may appear that no-one has died overnight, it may just be an effect of your ability. Watch for sudden deaths before dusk if good, and use it to your advantage if evil, as information will be poisoned for the players involved!"],"bluffing":[],"fighting":[],"examples":["The Mad Scientist is in play, and is evil. On Day 1, the Baron is executed. The Mad Scientist immediately brings them back to life, preventing the Oracle from receiving a 1 that night."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":50,"otherNightReminder":"The Mad Scientist chooses a dead player.","reminders":["It''s Alive!"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/sci.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/scig.png","imageAlt2":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/scie.png"}','published','the-menagerie/mad-scientist',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));